    "narrative": "The Austin Waves project a balanced offensive attack today, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (75.29) and **Andy Pages** (70.97), who both benefit from a highly favorable matchup against Brandon Pfaadt. **Kyle Tucker** serves as our primary offensive engine, with his score buoyed by strong park factors and platoon advantages, while **Andy Pages** climbs into elite territory due to his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries, offering significant stolen base upside. We also see high-ceiling potential from **Jacob Wilson** (69.79), whose matchup against Jake Bennett provides a rare combination of park favorability and platoon efficiency that allows him to outperform his base projection significantly.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was bypassing **Dominic Smith** (46.93) and **Sam Antonacci** (46.72). **Dominic Smith** was the closest to cracking the starting nine; while his park and wind advantages were notable, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to **Jorge Polanco** and **Nasim Nunez** to maintain defensive flexibility and maximize category coverage. We are navigating significant volatility today, as the entire lineup remains \"Lineup Pending,\" forcing us to rely on historical batting order assumptions. Risk remains elevated across the board, particularly for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Heliot Ramos**, both of whom are squaring off against elite arms in Jacob deGrom and Chris Sale, respectively. While **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a 14% boost due to dynamic platoon splits, his floor is compressed by the difficulty of the matchup, requiring us to monitor the late-afternoon weather and lineup confirmations closely to preserve our efficiency caps.",
